# The native Android project is GENERATED — `npx cap add android` (or
# build-release.sh / the CI workflow) recreates it from capacitor.config.json,
# so the package name always follows the appId. Committing it just adds noise
# and machine-specific SDK paths (android/local.properties).
android/
node_modules/

# Signing material — NEVER commit these. The keystore lives on your machine
# (and in CI as the ANDROID_KEYSTORE_BASE64 secret); losing it means you can
# never ship an update to an already-installed app.
*.keystore
*.jks
keystore.properties
